      "body": "https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/12fb7492-07c1-4d33-b045-e466415b5384\n\n### Update\n1. Wired it with a wedge menu and as we can see the following stuff which was initially asked in the PR is now being solved \n\nI've attached a short screen recording demonstrating the completed Duplicate wedge flow for #796.\n\nThe recording verifies:\n\n* Duplicating a brick creates an independent copy as a separate tower.\n* The selected brick and its subtree are duplicated correctly.\n* The original tower remains unchanged.\n* The duplicate can be interacted with independently.\n\n\nThe implementation has also been verified with the full test suite, lint, TypeScript checks, and `git diff --check`.\n\nEverything is working as expected from the UI side.\n\n",
